% ============================================================================
% celestial-object-alt-name.query.adj — a worked recall over the astronomy
% celestial-object-alt-name library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what else is a moon
% called?": it states no astronomy fact of its own — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?`
% against the `celestial_object_alt_name` rows and returns the alternate
% name + the table's source/locator/trust. An object the cited spans do not
% give a second name for abstains honestly — the engine never invents a
% synonym.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli celestial-object-alt-name.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "celestial-object-alt-name.adj"

? celestial_object_alt_name(moon, $AltName)      % expect planetary_satellites
? celestial_object_alt_name(asteroid, $AltName)  % expect minor_planets
? celestial_object_alt_name(star, $AltName)      % expect abstain — the cited span names no alternate term for star
